[TITLE]
InpWriter round-trip fixture: unresolvable link end node
The deliberate behaviour change that came with defect 10's fix. C1 names J_MISSING,
which no node section defines. Before the deferred pass this link loaded silently
orphaned (node2 == -1) with no diagnostic at all, and was then written back out
with a '*' ToNode. It is now a fatal ERROR 209, matching legacy link_readParams().

[OPTIONS]
FLOW_UNITS           CFS
INFILTRATION         HORTON
FLOW_ROUTING         DYNWAVE
START_DATE           01/01/2020
START_TIME           00:00:00
END_DATE             01/01/2020
END_TIME             01:00:00
REPORT_STEP          00:15:00
WET_STEP             00:05:00
DRY_STEP             01:00:00
ROUTING_STEP         0:00:30
MIN_SLOPE            0

[JUNCTIONS]
;;Name  Elev  MaxDepth  InitDepth  SurDepth  Aponded
J1       10.0  5.0       0          0         0

[OUTFALLS]
;;Name  Elev  Type  StageData  Gated
O1       8.0   FREE  *          NO

[CONDUITS]
;;Name  FromNode  ToNode      Length  Roughness  InOffset  OutOffset
C1       J1        J_MISSING   400.0   0.013      0         0
C2       J1        O1          400.0   0.013      0         0

[XSECTIONS]
;;Link  Shape     Geom1  Geom2  Geom3  Geom4  Barrels
C1       CIRCULAR  1.5    0      0      0      1
C2       CIRCULAR  1.5    0      0      0      1

[REPORT]
INPUT       NO
CONTROLS    NO
NODES       ALL
LINKS       ALL

[COORDINATES]
;;Node  X-Coord  Y-Coord
J1       0.0      0.0
O1       500.0    0.0
